    "body": "Child of #416 (decomposition approved by the maintainer on 2026-11-27; key `commit`, after: `plan-floor`). Decomposition: https://github.com/mintswarm/mintswarm/issues/416/artifacts/3\n\n## Problem\n\ncommit.py wraps foreign text in its GitError and Refusal messages:\n- \"cannot run …: {exc}\" (81);\n- \"cannot load …: {type}: {exc}\" (145);\n- \"yq gave no JSON …: {exc}\" (179);\n- \"cannot read …: {exc}\" (187);\n- \"formatter … cannot run: {exc}\" (308).\nIt also prints str(exc) at 383 and 386. It loads plan-approval/floor.py by path.\nhooks/pre-commit, a Python script, runs it.\n\n## Suggested approach\n\n- Derive GitError and Refusal from the shared base, with fixed causes raised\n  `from exc`. Use the fixed OS phrases.\n- Where a floor domain error reaches commit.py, carry its message.\n- Check hooks/pre-commit for the same pattern.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No change to what is staged, formatted or refused.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- No output line of commit.py or hooks/pre-commit contains third-party error text.\n- commit-selftest.py asserts on no third-party error wording.\n",
